---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Contact";
const description =
  "How to reach ListBulkly, what is available before launch, and where to report a security issue.";
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <p>
    ListBulkly is a small operation with one inbox. The same address handles
    support, privacy and data requests, billing and security reports, so nothing
    gets lost in a mailbox nobody reads. Put the topic in the subject line.
  </p>
  <p>
    The registered company name and postal address are not published yet, so this
    inbox is the only official contact.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Everything:</strong>
      <a href="mailto:listbulkly@gmail.com">listbulkly@gmail.com</a>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Support:</strong> subject "support"</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy or data request:</strong> subject "privacy" or "delete my account"</li>
    <li><strong>Billing:</strong> subject "billing"</li>
    <li><strong>Legal:</strong> subject "legal"</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security reports</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe you have found a vulnerability, please report it privately rather
    than opening a public issue: email
    <a href="mailto:listbulkly@gmail.com">listbulkly@gmail.com</a> with "security" in
    the subject. Include
    the page, the steps and what you observed. We will acknowledge a report and tell
    you whether it is in scope; we will not ask you to test against another seller's
    data.
  </p>

  <h2>What to include for a product bug</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>the page you were on and the button you pressed;</li>
    <li>the exact message shown (Printify's own message is passed through verbatim);</li>
    <li>whether the library was created in this browser or imported;</li>
    <li>your browser name and version.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Never send an API key in a support message. Keys are stored in your browser and
    can be cleared in Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal pages</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a> ·
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds</a> · <a href="/cookies">Cookies</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
